 "transcript": [
  "[action] eldest son leaves land with wife",
  "[action] Wang Lung watches his sons as they leave.",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"Well, and I am a man now and I have a wife and we live in a fine house and I am in the town with the rich men.\"",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) The second son laughs at his brother's complaints.",
  "[action] The eldest son watches his brother with a sly smile.",
  "[action] Wang Lung laughs at his sons' complaints.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what now? Am I never to be free in my house?\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and I am not so foolish to be a servant to my father any longer.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Now I have no son, and he is more like his mother in his pride.\"",
  "[action] (to the second son) Wang Lung calls his second son.",
  "Wang Lung (to the second son): \"Well, and what now, and have you no business to do?\"",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"There is a good deal of business this year, for the roads are clear and there are no floods and the harvest is good. There are men coming from a great house in the town.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"I have no business with these people in the town,\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and they are rich and they will give a good price for the wheat.\"",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung turns to his eldest son.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and I know that these are the people who own the land which I once farmed and I do not care to see them.\"",
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung commands his sons to bring the silver to him.",
  "[says] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung tells his sons to bring the silver.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Now bring me the silver, for I have business.\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and you are a fool to do so, and I shall not do it.\""
 ],
